WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.576
Learn to complete drawings of shapes to make them symmetrical and identify the lines

00:00:05.576 --> 00:00:09.800
of symmetry of regular and irregular 2d shapes (triangles and quadrilateral)

00:00:10.617 --> 00:00:15.837
A point is 16 squares below a horizontal mirror line. Where must its reflection be

00:00:15.837 --> 00:00:20.709
drawn? The answer is 16 squares above. A reflection stays the same distance across

00:00:20.709 --> 00:00:21.753
the mirror line.

00:00:22.617 --> 00:00:27.324
A dot is 8 squares left of a vertical mirror. Where should its reflected dot be?

00:00:27.324 --> 00:00:29.678
Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:30.533 --> 00:00:35.440
The answer is 8 squares right. Reflection keeps the same distance across the mirror.
